<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 802,173 tonnes of oilseed in February 1997 against 919,673 tonnes in February 1996, the Agriculture Secretariat said. (Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean		 357,198    (597,100)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 418,126    (294,448)</p>
<p> Linseed		   7,965     (23,672)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  18,884	(4,453)</p>
<p> Cottonseed		  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p>Output in February was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean	63,917    (107,061)    288,221     (482,634)</p>
<p> Sunflower   163,465    (116,949)    180,751     (127,336)</p>
<p> Linseed	 2,493	(7,757)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut     7,281	(2,034)     10,911	 (3,011)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	nil	  (nil)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    1,831   (3,253)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower    nil     (nil)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    5,196  (15,113)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to February, with the same period in 1996 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean		 868,568    (1,321,556)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 577,431	(502,071)</p>
<p> Linseed		  10,610	 (48,858)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  39,130	 (16,261)</p>
<p> Cottonseed		  nil	    (nil)</p>
<p>Output in January through February (1996 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     155,000    (239,699)    697,371  (1,078,158)</p>
<p> Sunflower   229,195,   (201,750)    249,921    (213,025)</p>
<p> Linseed	 8,800     (16,185)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    15,194	(6,474)     22,611	(9,755)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	nil	 (nil)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean     3,818  (5,365)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower     nil    (402)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed     6,967 (31,056)</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
</text>
